  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p>I’m thrilled to announce that <em><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet-cookbook/\">The How Not to Diet Cookbook</a> </em>is now available for preorder for everyone on your holiday gift list! If you have my first one, <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-die-cookbook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>The</em> <em>How Not to Die Cookbook</em></a>, you’ll recognize the one-and-only Robin Robertson joined me again to develop over 100 whole food, plant-based recipes inspired by cuisines around the world. Here’s a tiny sample of what’s in my new cookbook: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Red Bean and Butternut Caldo Verde</li>\n<li>Thai Green Papaya Salad</li>\n<li>Zucchini Linguini with Mushroom-Lentil Bolongese</li>\n<li>Jicama Nachos</li>\n<li>Black Forest Chia Pudding</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Not only is every recipe health-promoting, but every ingredient of every recipe is healthful. All recipes are composed of 100% Green-Light ingredients. But how do you make things sweet without sugar? Salty without salt? Those were some of the challenges that made creating the cookbook so much fun!</p>\n<p>Specific to the <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/trailer-for-how-not-to-diet-dr-gregers-guide-to-weight-loss/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">21 Tweaks</a> for evidence-based weight loss I detailed in <em><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How Not to Diet</a></em>, recipes include the foods that act as fat blockers and fat burners, and starch blockers and appetite suppressants, such as black cumin, vinegar, and my prebiotic BROL mixture. The recipes that meet my “negative calorie” preloading criteria are clearly marked. If you haven’t read <em><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How Not to Diet</a></em> yet, grab a copy from your local library or wherever you buy or borrow your books.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet-cookbook/\">Preorder your copy</a> of my new cookbook today, and books will be arriving December 8, just in time for the holidays and your New Year, New You resolutions.</p>\n<p><strong>Get a Signed Bookplate</strong><br/>\nFor a limited time, donate any amount to NutritionFacts.org using <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.z2systems.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=51&amp;&amp;test=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://nutritionfacts.z2systems.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=51&amp;&amp;test=true\">this form</a> to receive a signed bookplate to put in your copy as a thank you gift. The bookplates also make a great keepsake for any of your copies of <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>How Not to Diet</em></a>, <em><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/books/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How Not to Die</a>, </em>or<em> <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-die-cookbook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The How Not to Die Cookbook</a></em>. All proceeds go to keeping the 501(c)3 nonprofit organization NutritionFacts growing and going. Donate today since <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.z2systems.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=51&amp;&amp;test=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://nutritionfacts.z2systems.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=51&amp;&amp;test=true\">this form</a> will only be up until my hand cramps up. :)</p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Videos on Plant-Based Meats Available for Download</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/videos/products/plant-based-and-cultivated-meat-digital\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-65293 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Meat-AlternativesDownload-Artwork-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Meat-AlternativesDownload-Artwork-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Meat-AlternativesDownload-Artwork-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Meat-AlternativesDownload-Artwork-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Meat-AlternativesDownload-Artwork-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Meat-AlternativesDownload-Artwork-1200x1200.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Meat-AlternativesDownload-Artwork-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Meat-AlternativesDownload-Artwork-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Meat-AlternativesDownload-Artwork.png 2000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a></p>\n<p>Thank you to everyone who joined my recent webinar, The Human Health Implications of Plant-Based and Cultivated Meat for Pandemic Prevention and Climate Mitigation. The high-quality digital download of the videos from that webinar is now available on <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/videos/products/plant-based-and-cultivated-meat-digital\">DrGreger.org</a>. These videos will eventually be on NutritionFacts.org for free, but if you don’t want to wait, you can get them right now.</p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 class=\"null\">New Comment Platform Coming Soon</h4>\n<div><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-65298\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Green-Speach-Bubble.png\" alt=\"Green-Speech-Bubble\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Green-Speach-Bubble.png 1000w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Green-Speach-Bubble-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Green-Speach-Bubble-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Green-Speach-Bubble-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Green-Speach-Bubble-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Green-Speach-Bubble-540x540.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>Longtime users of NutritionFacts.org will be familiar with this change – we are returning to Disqus for the comments on the website. This will allow us to have more features that many of you have been requesting. You will be able to log in via Disqus.com, using your social media, or you can create and reply to comments without logging in at all. It also means that we will be saying goodbye to the user logins on NutritionFacts.org, so if you have any videos saved to your “favorites,” now is the time to save those links on your computer before the function goes away. These changes will be rolling out in the next few weeks. </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Just Ask Alexa!  </h4>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-65300\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Wellian-Dr.Greger-Newsletter-Picture-1024x754.png\" alt=\"Wellian-Dr.Greger\" width=\"201\" height=\"148\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Wellian-Dr.Greger-Newsletter-Picture-1024x754.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Wellian-Dr.Greger-Newsletter-Picture-960x707.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Wellian-Dr.Greger-Newsletter-Picture-768x565.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Wellian-Dr.Greger-Newsletter-Picture-1200x883.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Wellian-Dr.Greger-Newsletter-Picture-720x530.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Wellian-Dr.Greger-Newsletter-Picture-540x397.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Wellian-Dr.Greger-Newsletter-Picture.png 1826w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/>A company called Wellian has developed an Alexa app that lets you tap into NutritionFacts.org’s information straight from your Alexa device. Simply subscribe, activate the app, and ask questions like “What causes heart disease?” or “How to improve my immune system?” <a href=\"https://www.wellian.com/at-home-plans-drgreger-572ff5c0\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.wellian.com/at-home-plans-drgreger-572ff5c0\">Learn more about Wellian with Alexa</a>. I can’t wait to try it! </p>\n</div>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Doctor and Dietitian Q&amp;A</h4>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-65302 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Doctor-Dietitian-Q-A-IG-9-18-20-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Doctor-Dietitian-Q-A-IG-9-18-20-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Doctor-Dietitian-Q-A-IG-9-18-20-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Doctor-Dietitian-Q-A-IG-9-18-20-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Doctor-Dietitian-Q-A-IG-9-18-20-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Doctor-Dietitian-Q-A-IG-9-18-20-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Doctor-Dietitian-Q-A-IG-9-18-20-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/09/Doctor-Dietitian-Q-A-IG-9-18-20.png 1081w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>Join me for another live Instagram Q&amp;A with one of my favorite dietitians and dearest friends, <a href=\"https://plantbaseddietitian.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://plantbaseddietitian.com/\">Julieanna Hever</a>. <br/>\nHead over to the <a href=\"https://instagram.com/nutrition_facts_org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://instagram.com/nutrition_facts_org/\">NutritionFacts.org Instagram</a> page on <strong>9/18 at 3pm ET</strong> to get the answers to your health and nutrition questions.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-60211 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-vegetarians-really-have-higher-stroke-risk/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-63173\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-17-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Do Vegetarians Really Have Higher Stroke Risk?\" width=\"251\" height=\"141\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-17-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-17-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-17-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-17-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-17-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-17-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-17-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-17.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 251px) 100vw, 251px\"/></a></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-vegetarians-really-have-higher-stroke-risk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Do Vegetarians Really Have Higher Stroke Risk?</a></p>\n<p>The first study in history on the incidence of stroke of vegetarians and vegans suggests they may be at higher risk.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/vegetarians-and-stroke-risk-factors-vitamin-b12-homocysteine/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-64364\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/08/50-23-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Vegetarians and Stroke Risk Factors—Vitamin B12 &amp; Homocysteine?\" width=\"249\" height=\"140\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/08/50-23-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/08/50-23-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/08/50-23-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/08/50-23-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/08/50-23-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/08/50-23-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/08/50-23-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/08/50-23.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 249px) 100vw, 249px\"/></a></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/vegetarians-and-stroke-risk-factors-vitamin-b12-homocysteine/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Vegetarians and Stroke Risk Factors—B12 &amp; Homocysteine?</a></p>\n<p>Not taking B12 supplements or regularly eating B12 fortified foods may explain the higher stroke risk found among vegetarians.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-coconut-oil-and-abdominal-fat/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-63974\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/07/FBF-Coconut-Oil-and-Abdominal-Fat-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"249\" height=\"140\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/07/FBF-Coconut-Oil-and-Abdominal-Fat-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/07/FBF-Coconut-Oil-and-Abdominal-Fat-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/07/FBF-Coconut-Oil-and-Abdominal-Fat-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/07/FBF-Coconut-Oil-and-Abdominal-Fat-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/07/FBF-Coconut-Oil-and-Abdominal-Fat-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/07/FBF-Coconut-Oil-and-Abdominal-Fat-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/07/FBF-Coconut-Oil-and-Abdominal-Fat-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/07/FBF-Coconut-Oil-and-Abdominal-Fat.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 249px) 100vw, 249px\"/></a></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-coconut-oil-and-abdominal-fat/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Flashback Friday: Coconut Oil and Abdominal Fat</a></p>\n<p>What does a review of the evidence on the effects of coconut oil on weight loss and belly fat find?</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Live Q&amp;A on Sept 24</h4>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51462 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1200x1200.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-200x200.png 200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square-522x522.png 522w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2017/12/LiveQANewsletter-Square.png 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>Every month I do a live Q&amp;A from my treadmill, and this month <em><strong>Sept 24</strong></em> is the day.</p>\n<p>Join on our <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\">Facebook</a> page or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\">YouTube</a> channel at <strong>3pm ET</strong>.  I’ll be streaming to both at the same time!</p>\n<p>You can now find links to all of my past live Q&amp;As <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a> on NutritionFacts.org. If that’s not enough, remember I have an audio podcast to keep you company at <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\">nutritionfacts.org/audio</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
